Do not let a metrics-file failure terminate the SMP server. The periodic
savePrometheusMetrics thread races every other server thread in raceAny_;
when opening or writing the metrics path failed (for example while a lazy
reader in the same process still holds the file lock), the exception ended
this thread, raceAny_ cancelled the remaining server threads and all clients
were disconnected. Log the failure and keep serving; the next interval
retries the save. Async exceptions are unaffected, so shutdown still
cancels this thread normally.

Index: src/Simplex/Messaging/Server.hs
--- src/Simplex/Messaging/Server.hs.orig
+++ src/Simplex/Messaging/Server.hs
@@ -688,7 +688,12 @@
         ts <- getCurrentTime
         sm <- getServerMetrics st ss rtsOpts
         rtm <- getRealTimeMetrics env
-        T.writeFile metricsFile $ prometheusMetrics sm rtm ts
+        -- A transient metrics-file failure must not stop the SMP server: this
+        -- thread races every other server thread in raceAny_, so an uncaught
+        -- exception would cancel all server threads and disconnect clients.
+        E.try @E.IOException (T.writeFile metricsFile $ prometheusMetrics sm rtm ts) >>= \case
+          Left e -> logError $ "Error saving Prometheus metrics: " <> tshow e
+          Right _ -> pure ()
 
